CISF Alertness Leads to Detection of Exam Malpractice Devices at Goa Airport

Displaying exemplary alertness and vigilance, CISF personnel at Goa Airport detected suspected electronic devices linked to examination malpractice during passenger screening. Subsequent checks led to the interception of two passengers bound for Delhi and the recovery of 04 electronic devices, 03 SIM cards, 05 Bluetooth earpieces, an examination admit card and Aadhaar cards.

The matter was referred to IB and Military Intelligence for joint enquiry, which revealed suspected impersonation in connection with a recruitment examination conducted at IIT Goa. Both passengers, along with the recovered devices and documents, were handed over to the local police. An FIR has been registered, and further investigation is underway.

CISF remains vigilant in safeguarding aviation security through alert screening, timely detection and effective inter-agency coordination.

