🏆 CISF Secures 2nd Position in CTF LEA 2.0 at c0c0n 2026

CISF secured 2nd position in its maiden participation in CTF LEA 2.0 at c0c0n 2026 – The International Security and Hacking Conference, organised by Keralam Police in association with the Information Security Research Association.

The two-day challenge, held on 09–10 October, brought together leading State Police organisations, Intelligence Agencies, CAPFs and Law Enforcement Agencies from India and abroad to test their expertise in digital forensics, malware analysis, application security, OSINT, cryptography, cybercrime investigation and incident response.

The achievement marks a significant milestone in CISF’s efforts to strengthen its cybersecurity capabilities. The winners were felicitated by Sh. V. D. Satheesan, Hon’ble Chief Minister of Keralam, in the presence of senior police officials, international cybersecurity dignitaries and other distinguished guests.

Represented by Sh. Akshay Badola, Assistant Commandant, this achievement reflects CISF’s commitment to strengthening cyber preparedness and technological excellence.

